4:["$","main",null,{"className":"blog-page","children":[["$","$Le",null,{}],["$","article",null,{"className":"blog-article","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell blog-article-shell","children":[["$","$Lf",null,{"className":"blog-back-link","href":"/blog","children":[["$","$L10",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":16}]," All guides"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-tag","children":["Admissions"," · ","One Window archive"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"How to Write an SOP in 2026: Why Generic and AI-Written Statements Fail"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"blog-article-intro","children":"Your SOP cannot sound like ChatGPT wrote it. That may sound dramatic, but for 2026 applicants, it is a real concern. AI has changed the way students write. A clean-looking Statement of Purpose can now be generated in seconds. The grammar may be perfect. The vocabulary may sound impressive. The structure may look neat. But admissions teams are not only checking whether your English is polished. They are trying to understand something much harder: whether there is a real student behind the statement."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-article-body","children":[["$","section","How to Write an SOP in 2026: Why Generic and AI-Written Statements Fail",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"How to Write an SOP in 2026: Why Generic and AI-Written Statements Fail"}],[["$","p","And that is where many SOPs fail.",{"children":"And that is where many SOPs fail."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","Why This Matters More in 2026",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Why This Matters More in 2026"}],[["$","p","AI is no longer a small trend. OpenAI reported around 700 million weekly ChatGPT users in 2025. That means students applying in 2026 are writing in a world where AI-assisted writing is completely normal.",{"children":"AI is no longer a small trend. OpenAI reported around 700 million weekly ChatGPT users in 2025. That means students applying in 2026 are writing in a world where AI-assisted writing is completely normal."}],["$","p","Application volumes are also high. Common App reported that through January 1, 2026, application volume to returning members rose 7%, from about 7.08 million applications in 2024–25 to about 7.61 million in 2025–26.",{"children":"Application volumes are also high. Common App reported that through January 1, 2026, application volume to returning members rose 7%, from about 7.08 million applications in 2024–25 to about 7.61 million in 2025–26."}],["$","p","So admissions teams are not reading a few hundred personal essays in a quiet room. They are reviewing huge numbers of applications, many of which now sound more polished than before.",{"children":"So admissions teams are not reading a few hundred personal essays in a quiet room. They are reviewing huge numbers of applications, many of which now sound more polished than before."}],["$","p","That creates a strange problem: when everyone sounds polished, polish stops being impressive. What stands out is specificity.",{"children":"That creates a strange problem: when everyone sounds polished, polish stops being impressive. What stands out is specificity."}]],["$","ul",null,{"children":[]}]]}],["$","section","The Problem With Generic SOPs",{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"The Problem With Generic SOPs"}],[["$","p","Most weak SOPs do not fail because the student is weak. They fail because the writing is too broad. A generic SOP usually says things like:",{"children":"Most weak SOPs do not fail because the student is weak. They fail because the writing is too broad. A generic SOP usually says things like:"}]],"$L11"]}],"$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a"]}],"$L1b"]}]}],"$L1c"]}]
:HL["/Logos/OW%20web%20desktop%20logos%20(200%20x%2040%20px)/OW%20White%20Logo%20desktop.png","image"]
